From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:46:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: host: Report active mission-mode PM state

The PCI client restoring CE interrupts needs to distinguish an active
mission-mode host from a pending suspend or an error transition. Read
the host PM state and execution environment together under pm_lock.
The query is a snapshot and does not prevent a subsequent transition.

Codex adapted the fourth-batch check and built the affected ARM64
MHI module with the Piano configuration.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/mhi.h       |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c
index 832bd926e..7c16b4828 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pm.c
@@ -1058,6 +1058,22 @@ int mhi_pm_resume_force(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mhi_pm_resume_force);
 
+bool mhi_pm_is_active(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+	bool active;
+	u32 state;
+
+	read_lock_irqsave(&mhi_cntrl->pm_lock, flags);
+	state = mhi_cntrl->pm_state;
+	active = (state == MHI_PM_M0 || state == MHI_PM_M2) &&
+		 MHI_IN_MISSION_MODE(mhi_cntrl->ee);
+	read_unlock_irqrestore(&mhi_cntrl->pm_lock, flags);
+
+	return active;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mhi_pm_is_active);
+
 bool mhi_pm_is_suspended(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
 {
 	return MHI_PM_IN_SUSPEND_STATE(READ_ONCE(mhi_cntrl->pm_state));
diff --git a/include/linux/mhi.h b/include/linux/mhi.h
index 07166ab15..50d598db6 100644
--- a/include/linux/mhi.h
+++ b/include/linux/mhi.h
@@ -714,6 +714,15 @@ int mhi_pm_resume(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl);
  */
 int mhi_pm_resume_force(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl);
 
+/**
+ * mhi_pm_is_active - Check whether the host is active in mission mode
+ * @mhi_cntrl: MHI controller
+ *
+ * This is a snapshot of the software state. It does not wake the device or
+ * prevent a power or reset transition.
+ */
+bool mhi_pm_is_active(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl);
+
 /**
  * mhi_pm_is_suspended - Check whether the host is entering or retaining M3
  * @mhi_cntrl: MHI controller
-- 
